00:02:57.990 --> 00:02:59.910
So why should you focus on LinkedIn?

00:02:59.910 --> 00:03:02.760
If you want to build a
professional brand at the moment,

00:03:02.760 --> 00:03:04.860
and there are many things
I could talk about,

00:03:04.860 --> 00:03:08.490
let me focus on reach for
the purpose of this video.

00:03:08.490 --> 00:03:11.730
At the moment, even if you
are still a small account,

00:03:11.730 --> 00:03:13.200
you have the opportunity to reach

00:03:13.200 --> 00:03:16.290
a significant amount
of people on LinkedIn.

00:03:16.290 --> 00:03:18.660
And this might change over the next years,

00:03:18.660 --> 00:03:20.790
maybe, maybe not, but at the moment,

00:03:20.790 --> 00:03:22.170
that's for sure the case.

00:03:22.170 --> 00:03:24.060
Let's compare that to another platform,

00:03:24.060 --> 00:03:25.590
for instance, Facebook.

00:03:25.590 --> 00:03:26.880
So let's say you have a Facebook

00:03:26.880 --> 00:03:29.700
profile with 1,000 followers.

00:03:29.700 --> 00:03:33.300
Well, if you release a post
without boosting it with ads,

00:03:33.300 --> 00:03:36.900
likely only a fraction of
these followers will see that.

00:03:36.900 --> 00:03:39.510
Let's just say roughly 5%.

00:03:39.510 --> 00:03:42.780
So for 1,000 followers,
maybe your posts on average,

00:03:42.780 --> 00:03:44.550
will get about 50 views,

00:03:44.550 --> 00:03:46.530
just the fraction of your audience.

00:03:46.530 --> 00:03:49.410
This is very different
right now on LinkedIn.

00:03:49.410 --> 00:03:51.450
If you have thousand followers,

00:03:51.450 --> 00:03:56.247
you can expect that your posts
will be seen by 2,000 people.

00:03:56.247 --> 00:03:58.680
You can expect that a
multiple of your followers,

00:03:58.680 --> 00:04:00.690
will regularly see your content.

00:04:00.690 --> 00:04:02.610
And this is of course a very great

00:04:02.610 --> 00:04:04.290
and significant opportunity.

00:04:04.290 --> 00:04:06.930
And there are only very
few platforms at the moment

00:04:06.930 --> 00:04:09.270
out there that will give
you a comparable reach.

00:04:09.270 --> 00:04:11.550
Let us substantiate this
with some action numbers

00:04:11.550 --> 00:04:14.070
and for data, I prepared some
data from my own account.

00:04:14.070 --> 00:04:16.800
I was that I also used
for my Firm Learning work.

00:04:16.800 --> 00:04:19.290
This was data point until
the end of the first half

00:04:19.290 --> 00:04:20.123
of this year.

00:04:20.123 --> 00:04:23.130
At that point in time, I
had about 18,000 followers.

00:04:23.130 --> 00:04:25.620
And if I just took the
median post of all the posts

00:04:25.620 --> 00:04:29.610
that I created, the median
post got about 30,000 views,

00:04:29.610 --> 00:04:31.709
which is roughly two times the followers

00:04:31.709 --> 00:04:33.420
that I had at that time.

00:04:33.420 --> 00:04:37.350
But there was also post
that received 188,000 views

00:04:37.350 --> 00:04:38.460
at that point in time.

00:04:38.460 --> 00:04:41.250
So this is 10X, the followers that I had.

00:04:41.250 --> 00:04:44.062
So this illustrates the
opportunities that are out there.

00:04:44.062 --> 00:04:45.960
And I will talk more
about how to write exactly

00:04:45.960 --> 00:04:47.910
these types of posts in a moment.

00:04:47.910 --> 00:04:49.290
The second question that I often get is

00:04:49.290 --> 00:04:51.870
whether I should post on my company page,

00:04:51.870 --> 00:04:54.090
if you have one or on
your personal profile,

00:04:54.090 --> 00:04:56.040
but if you're just an
individual, chances are higher

00:04:56.040 --> 00:04:58.260
you only have your personal
profile available anyways.

00:04:58.260 --> 00:05:02.610
But the good news is that
LinkedIn favors personal profiles

00:05:02.610 --> 00:05:04.617
over a company pages
when it comes to reach.

00:05:04.617 --> 00:05:06.330
And of course, the reasons for that are,

00:05:06.330 --> 00:05:07.860
I'd say rather obvious, of course,

00:05:07.860 --> 00:05:09.540
LinkedIn would love that the companies

00:05:09.540 --> 00:05:12.870
rather pay ads, pay ad
money to boost their posts.

00:05:12.870 --> 00:05:14.550
Whereas that's not that much of an option

00:05:14.550 --> 00:05:16.890
for personal individuals,
but he just as an example,

00:05:16.890 --> 00:05:18.953
the case of Volkswagen.

00:05:18.953 --> 00:05:20.520
So Volkswagen, the company Volkswagen

00:05:20.520 --> 00:05:22.470
has about 1.2 million followers,

00:05:22.470 --> 00:05:24.030
and they just picked a post of them

00:05:24.030 --> 00:05:26.490
that just got a couple of hundred likes.

00:05:26.490 --> 00:05:28.457
And if you contrast that to Herbert Diess

00:05:28.457 --> 00:05:31.650
one he recently was the
managing director of Volkswagen,

00:05:31.650 --> 00:05:34.380
even though he had less
than 300,000 views,

00:05:34.380 --> 00:05:37.650
his posts regularly get
over a thousand likes.

00:05:37.650 --> 00:05:39.960
And of course there's some
variants among these posts,

00:05:39.960 --> 00:05:41.400
but this is the general picture

00:05:41.400 --> 00:05:43.020
that you see almost everywhere.

00:05:43.020 --> 00:05:45.210
Personal profiles
definitely get more reach

00:05:45.210 --> 00:05:46.670
than company profiles on LinkedIn.

00:05:46.670 --> 00:05:48.210
So I definitely would encourage you

00:05:48.210 --> 00:05:49.770
to use your personal profile as well.

00:05:49.770 --> 00:05:50.700
And last but not least,

00:05:50.700 --> 00:05:53.190
it seems very clear to me that
the development of LinkedIn

00:05:53.190 --> 00:05:55.590
into an influencer and creator platform

00:05:55.590 --> 00:05:58.890
is a key strategic objective of LinkedIn.

00:05:58.890 --> 00:06:00.390
They're actively pushing it.

00:06:00.390 --> 00:06:02.700
You can see it with all the
initiatives that the company

00:06:02.700 --> 00:06:03.652
is coming up with.

00:06:03.652 --> 00:06:05.520
For instance, the top
voices award that now

00:06:05.520 --> 00:06:07.110
they award on a yearly basis.

00:06:07.110 --> 00:06:09.750
If you ever felt like you
wanted to build an influence

00:06:09.750 --> 00:06:12.780
on Instagram, on YouTube or
any of these other platforms,

00:06:12.780 --> 00:06:14.670
but you were just too late.

00:06:14.670 --> 00:06:17.040
Now it's your opportunity with LinkedIn.

00:06:17.040 --> 00:06:18.540
Because if you start now,

00:06:18.540 --> 00:06:21.960
you will definitely be still
early in the development

00:06:21.960 --> 00:06:23.820
of LinkedIn as a creator platform,

00:06:23.820 --> 00:06:26.730
the opportunities are out there,
you just need to grab them.

00:06:26.730 --> 00:06:29.280
So let's next talk about
the LinkedIn algorithm

00:06:29.280 --> 00:06:31.557
and why should you even care about how

00:06:31.557 --> 00:06:33.930
the LinkedIn algorithm works

00:06:33.930 --> 00:06:35.550
But in here again, I just looked at some

00:06:35.550 --> 00:06:38.760
of my own personal data on
my Heinrich Rusche profile.

00:06:38.760 --> 00:06:40.920
This is again the data
from the first half year

00:06:40.920 --> 00:06:41.880
of this year.

00:06:41.880 --> 00:06:45.360
And it just ordered all
the posts by the views

00:06:45.360 --> 00:06:46.620
that they received.

00:06:46.620 --> 00:06:50.640
And you can see that there's
quite a significant variance.

00:06:50.640 --> 00:06:51.690
On the left hand side,

00:06:51.690 --> 00:06:55.050
there are some posts that
got less than 10,000 views.

00:06:55.050 --> 00:06:58.260
Again, let me remind you I
had about 18,000 followers

00:06:58.260 --> 00:06:59.550
at that point in time.

00:06:59.550 --> 00:07:00.990
But then on the right hand side,

00:07:00.990 --> 00:07:05.990
I had a handful of posts
that exceeded 100,000 views

00:07:06.030 --> 00:07:09.033
and my most successful post
measured in views received,

00:07:09.033 --> 00:07:13.980
as I just also told you
earlier about 188,000 views,

00:07:13.980 --> 00:07:15.930
and of course views matters because

00:07:15.930 --> 00:07:17.430
if people don't see your content.

00:07:17.430 --> 00:07:19.530
You cannot really spread the messages

00:07:19.530 --> 00:07:20.580
that you want to spread.

00:07:20.580 --> 00:07:23.220
You cannot really work towards
the goals and objectives

00:07:23.220 --> 00:07:25.440
that you set for yourself
in the beginning.

00:07:25.440 --> 00:07:27.630
And of course, if people
don't find your posts,

00:07:27.630 --> 00:07:29.370
they also cannot find your profile.

00:07:29.370 --> 00:07:32.250
And therefore you also cannot
grow your follower base

00:07:32.250 --> 00:07:33.083
and your audience.

00:07:33.083 --> 00:07:35.700
So let's look at how the
LinkedIn algorithm works

00:07:35.700 --> 00:07:36.750
behind the scenes.

00:07:36.750 --> 00:07:39.810
And this is very similar
to almost all the other

00:07:39.810 --> 00:07:42.540
social media platform
algorithms work as well.

00:07:42.540 --> 00:07:44.670
And I can imagine this to
work is that at the beginning,

00:07:44.670 --> 00:07:48.120
if you post something LinkedIn
in the first minutes, hours,

00:07:48.120 --> 00:07:48.953
and so on,

00:07:48.953 --> 00:07:52.530
will show this post to a
fraction of your audience,

00:07:52.530 --> 00:07:54.420
to a fraction of your followers,

00:07:54.420 --> 00:07:56.010
or to a fraction of the people

00:07:56.010 --> 00:07:59.220
who usually enjoy the
content that you create.

00:07:59.220 --> 00:08:01.590
And then they observe what happens.

00:08:01.590 --> 00:08:03.780
Are these people spending
time on the post?

00:08:03.780 --> 00:08:06.810
Are they engaging with the post?
Are they leaving a comment?

00:08:06.810 --> 00:08:09.090
So they have all these types of indicators

00:08:09.090 --> 00:08:11.430
that let the algorithm
come to the conclusion,

00:08:11.430 --> 00:08:13.830
whether this is a good post or not.

00:08:13.830 --> 00:08:15.960
And so if this post performed well

00:08:15.960 --> 00:08:19.470
in this very close group of
your most engaged followers,

00:08:19.470 --> 00:08:21.240
then LinkedIn will likely show this post

00:08:21.240 --> 00:08:22.980
to an extended group of your followers

00:08:22.980 --> 00:08:25.020
to almost every one of your followers.

00:08:25.020 --> 00:08:27.300
And will look again, how is it performing?

00:08:27.300 --> 00:08:29.610
Is this performing well or not?

00:08:29.610 --> 00:08:32.130
And again, if even with
this extended group,

00:08:32.130 --> 00:08:33.780
LinkedIn comes to the conclusion that yes,

00:08:33.780 --> 00:08:36.810
it's a good post then likely
it will show this post

00:08:36.810 --> 00:08:38.160
to even more people.

00:08:38.160 --> 00:08:40.200
Often also not even
your followers anymore,

00:08:40.200 --> 00:08:42.480
but maybe people who LinkedIn believes

00:08:42.480 --> 00:08:45.990
to have similar interests than
the people who follow you,

00:08:45.990 --> 00:08:48.300
people who are similar to your followers.

00:08:48.300 --> 00:08:51.000
And then again, regard
interest, are they interested?

00:08:51.000 --> 00:08:53.490
Are they engaging? Are
they enjoying the post?

00:08:53.490 --> 00:08:55.740
And then based on that step by step,

00:08:55.740 --> 00:08:59.220
LinkedIn will show the
post to even more people

00:08:59.220 --> 00:09:00.720
up until the point where LinkedIn

00:09:00.720 --> 00:09:03.990
just doesn't find any
pockets of people anymore,

00:09:03.990 --> 00:09:06.150
where the LinkedIn
algorithm would be confident

00:09:06.150 --> 00:09:09.270
that these people would
enjoy your post as well.

00:09:09.270 --> 00:09:12.210
And of course, sometimes
there are these unicorn posts

00:09:12.210 --> 00:09:14.220
where the algorithm
comes to the conclusion

00:09:14.220 --> 00:09:16.500
that actually more or less
everyone would enjoy it,

00:09:16.500 --> 00:09:18.090
more or less everyone likes it.

00:09:18.090 --> 00:09:21.240
And then sometimes you have
these super viral posts

00:09:21.240 --> 00:09:22.980
that are seen by hundred thousands,

00:09:22.980 --> 00:09:25.170
if not millions of people.

00:09:25.170 --> 00:09:27.180
It's of course, very difficult to predict

00:09:27.180 --> 00:09:28.440
to write something like this,

00:09:28.440 --> 00:09:31.470
but occasionally this might happen to you.

00:09:31.470 --> 00:09:33.840
So what exactly are these
signals that the algorithm

00:09:33.840 --> 00:09:35.280
takes into consideration?

00:09:35.280 --> 00:09:36.900
And what's here important for me to say

00:09:36.900 --> 00:09:40.230
is though that I don't
have any inside knowledge

00:09:40.230 --> 00:09:43.170
behind the same knowledge
of how the algorithm works.

00:09:43.170 --> 00:09:45.210
The algorithm is first of all secret.

00:09:45.210 --> 00:09:48.090
And second, it constantly changes.

00:09:48.090 --> 00:09:50.640
What these are, are just
some common assumptions

00:09:50.640 --> 00:09:52.200
where people test the things,

00:09:52.200 --> 00:09:54.480
and this is what you
will find on many places

00:09:54.480 --> 00:09:56.670
on the internet that this is how it works,

00:09:56.670 --> 00:09:58.260
but it's definitely fair for yourself

00:09:58.260 --> 00:09:59.610
to run your own experiment,

00:09:59.610 --> 00:10:02.400
to see what really benefits
your specific account.

00:10:02.400 --> 00:10:04.770
So let's talk about some positive signals.

00:10:04.770 --> 00:10:05.603
First,

00:10:05.603 --> 00:10:08.610
one of the most important
things is time on post.

00:10:08.610 --> 00:10:11.220
One of the key metrics
that all of these platforms

00:10:11.220 --> 00:10:13.410
are optimizing is to keep people,

00:10:13.410 --> 00:10:16.380
keep users on the platform
for as long as possible.

00:10:16.380 --> 00:10:18.764
Because of course the longer
people spend on the platform,

00:10:18.764 --> 00:10:21.690
the more ads can be shown to these people.

00:10:21.690 --> 00:10:24.720
And this is usually one of the
biggest monetization levers

00:10:24.720 --> 00:10:26.130
that the platforms have.

00:10:26.130 --> 00:10:28.410
So time on post is key,

00:10:28.410 --> 00:10:31.740
but then of course, sharing
a post is a positive as well.

00:10:31.740 --> 00:10:33.930
Because if you share a
post to your network,

00:10:33.930 --> 00:10:36.270
you are saying that,
"Hey, this post is great.

00:10:36.270 --> 00:10:37.103
It's important.

00:10:37.103 --> 00:10:39.210
It's worth seeing and worth reading."

00:10:39.210 --> 00:10:40.860
Next, commenting.

00:10:40.860 --> 00:10:42.510
So LinkedIn wants to be the platform

00:10:42.510 --> 00:10:44.490
where people engage with each other,

00:10:44.490 --> 00:10:46.770
have conversations about topics,

00:10:46.770 --> 00:10:48.930
and comments definitely
work towards this goal.

00:10:48.930 --> 00:10:51.000
It's a key metric of engagement.

00:10:51.000 --> 00:10:54.150
Next, sending a post, you can
send a post to other users,

00:10:54.150 --> 00:10:54.983
to other people.

00:10:54.983 --> 00:10:56.700
This is a positive
sign, of course as well,

00:10:56.700 --> 00:10:58.020
because thereby you indicate

00:10:58.020 --> 00:10:59.970
that it's worth sending and sharing.

00:10:59.970 --> 00:11:00.803
Of course,

00:11:00.803 --> 00:11:03.090
if people follow your profile
after they read your post,

00:11:03.090 --> 00:11:04.890
this speaks towards the post as well.

00:11:04.890 --> 00:11:08.340
And of course, liking a post
also liking other comments

00:11:08.340 --> 00:11:10.440
will increase engagement in the same way.

00:11:10.440 --> 00:11:12.720
And then of course there are
negative signals as well.

00:11:12.720 --> 00:11:14.820
So of course, a big
negative signals already

00:11:14.820 --> 00:11:17.940
of these positive don't
exist and out there.

00:11:17.940 --> 00:11:19.890
But then surely if people hide the posts,

00:11:19.890 --> 00:11:20.850
or tell the platform

00:11:20.850 --> 00:11:22.860
that they don't want to
see content like this.

00:11:22.860 --> 00:11:24.150
This is very negative.

00:11:24.150 --> 00:11:26.970
If they unfollow you after
they read something from you,

00:11:26.970 --> 00:11:27.867
if they mute the post from you/

00:11:27.867 --> 00:11:31.694
Also, if they report the
post that you created,

00:11:31.694 --> 00:11:35.400
these of course, negative
signals from the algorithm.

00:11:35.400 --> 00:11:38.310
And if so far you received
any value from this video,

00:11:38.310 --> 00:11:40.740
please hit the like
button for the algorithm,

00:11:40.740 --> 00:11:43.200
and also follow or
subscribe to stay up to date

00:11:43.200 --> 00:11:44.130
on all my content.

00:11:44.130 --> 00:11:46.410
I will talk more about this going forward.

00:11:46.410 --> 00:11:48.360
So would love you to stay on board here.

00:11:48.360 --> 00:11:50.100
Next, let's talk about some little tips,

00:11:50.100 --> 00:11:52.230
that you can do to improve your profile.

00:11:52.230 --> 00:11:54.960
Especially with the goal
of becoming a creator.

00:11:54.960 --> 00:11:55.793
And first of all,

00:11:55.793 --> 00:11:58.440
I would encourage you to
use a background picture.

00:11:58.440 --> 00:12:00.840
Many profiles still don't
use background pictures,

00:12:00.840 --> 00:12:03.180
but if someone visits your
profile the first time,

00:12:03.180 --> 00:12:05.628
for instance, after having
seen a post on their feed,

00:12:05.628 --> 00:12:07.140
the background picture

00:12:07.140 --> 00:12:09.750
is what really gives
your profile character.

00:12:09.750 --> 00:12:12.570
And you can use it to
directly brand yourself,

00:12:12.570 --> 00:12:14.970
make sure that the key
messages are transported,

00:12:14.970 --> 00:12:16.680
and make sure that people
directly understand

00:12:16.680 --> 00:12:18.330
what you are all about,

00:12:18.330 --> 00:12:20.250
what they can expect if they follow you.

00:12:20.250 --> 00:12:21.810
Next is the tagline.

00:12:21.810 --> 00:12:23.400
So the tagline is the line

00:12:23.400 --> 00:12:25.380
that is this displayed below your name.

00:12:25.380 --> 00:12:26.760
The tagline is very important

00:12:26.760 --> 00:12:30.120
because it's shown across
many places on the platform.

00:12:30.120 --> 00:12:33.510
So usually whenever you write
a post, below your name,

00:12:33.510 --> 00:12:36.120
there will also be the tagline present.

00:12:36.120 --> 00:12:39.360
So this gives the first impression,
what is your background?

00:12:39.360 --> 00:12:40.560
What are you all about?

00:12:40.560 --> 00:12:43.020
Why should people be
interested in yourself?

00:12:43.020 --> 00:12:45.930
So make it as concise and
as punchy as possible,

00:12:45.930 --> 00:12:47.640
and avoid using too many words.

00:12:47.640 --> 00:12:48.840
Next are hashtags.

00:12:48.840 --> 00:12:50.490
So if you turn on the creator mode,

00:12:50.490 --> 00:12:51.870
I will show you what this is in a moment.

00:12:51.870 --> 00:12:54.150
You have the opportunity to add hashtags

00:12:54.150 --> 00:12:56.010
like this on your profile.

00:12:56.010 --> 00:12:59.190
This again helps the algorithm
to understand what the niches

00:12:59.190 --> 00:13:02.040
that you're talking about, what
topics you are focusing on.

00:13:02.040 --> 00:13:04.140
This is also called your authority

00:13:04.140 --> 00:13:07.110
and will also help the
LinkedIn search to place you

00:13:07.110 --> 00:13:08.430
in the appropriate search results.

00:13:08.430 --> 00:13:12.000
For this last panel, least make
use of the featured section.

00:13:12.000 --> 00:13:13.560
So LinkedIn provides you with a section

00:13:13.560 --> 00:13:16.380
where you can hand select certain posts

00:13:16.380 --> 00:13:18.810
that you feel like very well represent

00:13:18.810 --> 00:13:20.850
what's going on on your
page, what you're doing,

00:13:20.850 --> 00:13:22.260
what you're writing about,

00:13:22.260 --> 00:13:24.300
the signature pieces of content

00:13:24.300 --> 00:13:25.890
that you created in the past.

00:13:25.890 --> 00:13:26.820
Make use of that.

00:13:26.820 --> 00:13:27.660
Because again,

00:13:27.660 --> 00:13:30.180
this is the ideal place to
give the first impression

00:13:30.180 --> 00:13:32.280
to people who are new
to your personal brand,

00:13:32.280 --> 00:13:33.570
are new to your profile,

00:13:33.570 --> 00:13:35.160
to understand what you are all about.

00:13:35.160 --> 00:13:37.977
Let's now also talk about the
creator mode on your profile.

00:13:37.977 --> 00:13:41.790
You should find the option
to turn on the creator mode.

00:13:41.790 --> 00:13:44.310
This will give you access
to some additional features

00:13:44.310 --> 00:13:46.680
that are very relevant to creators.

00:13:46.680 --> 00:13:48.540
So I would definitely
recommend you to do that.

00:13:48.540 --> 00:13:50.400
For instance, you have
access to these hashtags

00:13:50.400 --> 00:13:51.930
that I showed you a moment ago.

00:13:51.930 --> 00:13:53.760
And another thing that
automatically happens

00:13:53.760 --> 00:13:55.320
if you turn on the creator mode,

00:13:55.320 --> 00:13:58.380
is that the main call to
action on your profile

00:13:58.380 --> 00:14:01.530
changes from connect to follow.

00:14:01.530 --> 00:14:03.630
So usually on standard profiles,

00:14:03.630 --> 00:14:05.580
people see the connect button

00:14:05.580 --> 00:14:07.290
so people can connect with the person,

00:14:07.290 --> 00:14:09.240
but then of course the other person needs

00:14:09.240 --> 00:14:11.178
to accept this connection
request this way.

00:14:11.178 --> 00:14:13.320
Follow means that the people

00:14:13.320 --> 00:14:15.900
want to see your content,
want to see your posts,

00:14:15.900 --> 00:14:18.870
but the other person doesn't
need to approve that.

00:14:18.870 --> 00:14:20.700
So the hurdles are lower.

00:14:20.700 --> 00:14:23.580
People are not afraid that
maybe you won't accept them.

00:14:23.580 --> 00:14:26.490
So if you change the
call to action to Follow,

00:14:26.490 --> 00:14:29.820
this will enable and encourage
more people to follow you.

00:14:29.820 --> 00:14:32.040
And therefore for you
to grow your audience,

00:14:32.040 --> 00:14:34.080
of course, people can
still connect with you,

00:14:34.080 --> 00:14:36.420
but this will not be
the main call to action

00:14:36.420 --> 00:14:38.100
displayed on your profile anymore.

00:14:38.100 --> 00:14:40.410
Let's now talk about the content strategy.

00:14:40.410 --> 00:14:42.900
And in this section, I want
to talk about some tips,

00:14:42.900 --> 00:14:43.733
some advice,

00:14:43.733 --> 00:14:46.560
some little tactics and
hacks that you can use

00:14:46.560 --> 00:14:48.810
to really create the best possible content

00:14:48.810 --> 00:14:51.570
for the platform and maximize your chances

00:14:51.570 --> 00:14:53.400
to eventually create some content pieces

00:14:53.400 --> 00:14:56.430
that will also go viral and
thereby blow up your account.

00:14:56.430 --> 00:14:57.960
And what's important in the very beginning

00:14:57.960 --> 00:15:00.300
is that you should think about a niche,

00:15:00.300 --> 00:15:02.970
a topic that you want to stand for.

00:15:02.970 --> 00:15:04.800
So if people think about you,

00:15:04.800 --> 00:15:06.840
what do they want to have in mind?

00:15:06.840 --> 00:15:09.120
What are the key topics that you want

00:15:09.120 --> 00:15:11.220
to associate yourself with?

00:15:11.220 --> 00:15:13.140
So this is called your niche

00:15:13.140 --> 00:15:15.180
and this should be rather specific.

00:15:15.180 --> 00:15:18.150
You don't necessarily,
from the very first day,

00:15:18.150 --> 00:15:21.060
need to have a very tangible
first niche in mind.

00:15:21.060 --> 00:15:22.950
I think it's also fair just to start

00:15:22.950 --> 00:15:25.470
with more generic content
and then over time

00:15:25.470 --> 00:15:27.570
converge towards a niche.

00:15:27.570 --> 00:15:29.070
But in the medium term,

00:15:29.070 --> 00:15:31.080
you should develop this for yourself,

00:15:31.080 --> 00:15:32.040
because think about it,

00:15:32.040 --> 00:15:35.340
if you follow someone, why
are you following a profile?

00:15:35.340 --> 00:15:39.270
Because you want to read
more of this type of content,

00:15:39.270 --> 00:15:41.760
but if the content of a
person is all over the place

00:15:41.760 --> 00:15:43.440
changes all the time,

00:15:43.440 --> 00:15:45.540
why should someone follow you?

00:15:45.540 --> 00:15:48.480
So think about your niche
first and then from your niche

00:15:48.480 --> 00:15:50.880
you can then derive the content pieces

00:15:50.880 --> 00:15:52.170
that you want to create.

00:15:52.170 --> 00:15:55.500
And let's now start by
talking about the anatomy

00:15:55.500 --> 00:15:58.470
of a successful post on LinkedIn.

00:15:58.470 --> 00:16:00.390
And let's start with the hook.

00:16:00.390 --> 00:16:03.120
The post should always
start with the hook.

00:16:03.120 --> 00:16:05.193
So these are often one or two sentences

00:16:05.193 --> 00:16:08.280
that just spark interest, create interest.

00:16:08.280 --> 00:16:11.550
Let people want to read
more about the post.

00:16:11.550 --> 00:16:13.530
Let's remember the time on post

00:16:13.530 --> 00:16:15.750
is one of the most important indicators

00:16:15.750 --> 00:16:17.250
for the LinkedIn algorithm.

00:16:17.250 --> 00:16:19.080
So you want to excite people.

00:16:19.080 --> 00:16:21.840
You want to motivate people
to read all the post,

00:16:21.840 --> 00:16:24.420
because this is what will
get your time on post.

00:16:24.420 --> 00:16:26.550
After the hook, there's the body,

00:16:26.550 --> 00:16:29.250
and in this body in the
main part of your post,

00:16:29.250 --> 00:16:33.120
you should always focus
on communicating value,

00:16:33.120 --> 00:16:35.430
on communicating some insights,

00:16:35.430 --> 00:16:37.770
things that other people can take away,

00:16:37.770 --> 00:16:39.780
can learn from what you're writing about.

00:16:39.780 --> 00:16:41.760
This is at least the rule of thumb.

00:16:41.760 --> 00:16:44.430
You might occasionally deviate from that,

00:16:44.430 --> 00:16:47.280
but the majority of your
posts should be based

00:16:47.280 --> 00:16:48.113
on this framework.

00:16:48.113 --> 00:16:49.170
What many people do wrong,

00:16:49.170 --> 00:16:51.960
is that the write posts
completely self-centered,

00:16:51.960 --> 00:16:54.900
just about themselves,
about their business,

00:16:54.900 --> 00:16:57.570
all the great things that
they did in the past.

00:16:57.570 --> 00:16:58.440
That's boring.

00:16:58.440 --> 00:17:00.090
People don't want to read them,

00:17:00.090 --> 00:17:02.340
make it about the value
that you can deliver

00:17:02.340 --> 00:17:03.480
to the other person.

00:17:03.480 --> 00:17:04.917
Next around the end of the post

00:17:04.917 --> 00:17:06.810
end with the call to action.

00:17:06.810 --> 00:17:08.580
So ask people to do something.

00:17:08.580 --> 00:17:11.760
Here's also fair to vary these
call to actions over time.

00:17:11.760 --> 00:17:14.160
Maybe encourage people to leave a comment,

00:17:14.160 --> 00:17:16.230
'cause this, of course, sparks engagement,

00:17:16.230 --> 00:17:18.720
or you can encourage
people to follow your page,

00:17:18.720 --> 00:17:19.860
if they want to read more

00:17:19.860 --> 00:17:22.230
about this specific
type of content, right?

00:17:22.230 --> 00:17:23.610
So leave a call to action,

00:17:23.610 --> 00:17:25.530
encourage people to do
something, because again,

00:17:25.530 --> 00:17:27.780
this will also favor you in the algorithm.

00:17:27.780 --> 00:17:30.210
Now I don't want to talk
about hashtags too much here

00:17:30.210 --> 00:17:31.043
in this video.

00:17:31.043 --> 00:17:33.180
I trust you're familiar with
them from other platforms.

00:17:33.180 --> 00:17:35.160
The last thing that I
wanna talk about is that

00:17:35.160 --> 00:17:37.830
it's quite striking that
at least at the moment

00:17:37.830 --> 00:17:41.220
in the LinkedIn algorithm
posts that have an attachment.

00:17:41.220 --> 00:17:43.020
So some type of picture, for instance,

00:17:43.020 --> 00:17:45.390
or a slideshow or video
or anything like that,

00:17:45.390 --> 00:17:48.510
they tend to perform significantly better

00:17:48.510 --> 00:17:50.250
in the LinkedIn algorithm.

00:17:50.250 --> 00:17:53.340
So I just looked at my top
10 best performing posts

00:17:53.340 --> 00:17:56.610
and eight of these top
10 best performing posts

00:17:56.610 --> 00:17:58.890
had some type of picture attached to them.

00:17:58.890 --> 00:17:59.723
So in general,

00:17:59.723 --> 00:18:01.740
I would recommend you
to always use a picture.

00:18:01.740 --> 00:18:03.390
If you struggle to come up with a picture

00:18:03.390 --> 00:18:05.490
that really meets the message of the post,

00:18:05.490 --> 00:18:06.330
what many people do

00:18:06.330 --> 00:18:09.150
is just include a random
picture of themselves.

00:18:09.150 --> 00:18:11.464
And they just attach such
a picture of themselves

00:18:11.464 --> 00:18:12.570
to the post.

00:18:12.570 --> 00:18:15.690
I tried this out myself and
I can just only say it works.

00:18:15.690 --> 00:18:18.930
It significantly improves
the reach of your content.

00:18:18.930 --> 00:18:20.910
So let's now deep dive on the hook.

00:18:20.910 --> 00:18:21.832
So on the first sentences
that you leave on your post.

00:18:21.832 --> 00:18:24.336
Here, what you need to understand

00:18:24.336 --> 00:18:26.499
that after a couple of lines

00:18:26.499 --> 00:18:29.370
there is the so-called fold.

00:18:29.370 --> 00:18:32.340
So LinkedIn only shows
the beginning of the post

00:18:32.340 --> 00:18:34.327
and after a couple of
lines, then it just says,

00:18:34.327 --> 00:18:36.780
"see more" and people need
to click on "see more"

00:18:36.780 --> 00:18:38.520
to see the remainder of the post.

00:18:38.520 --> 00:18:40.860
So here what's important is
that you're able to place

00:18:40.860 --> 00:18:42.750
the full hook before the fold,

00:18:42.750 --> 00:18:45.360
make sure the full hook is seen before

00:18:45.360 --> 00:18:46.590
then this fold arrives.

00:18:46.590 --> 00:18:49.950
And the good thing is that
where this fold is placed

00:18:49.950 --> 00:18:51.450
is predictable.

00:18:51.450 --> 00:18:52.830
And it depends on whether

00:18:52.830 --> 00:18:55.530
there is an attachment to the post or not.

00:18:55.530 --> 00:18:56.910
And if you follow the recommendation

00:18:56.910 --> 00:18:58.350
that I just gave you a moment ago,

00:18:58.350 --> 00:19:00.840
you will almost always
have such an attachment

00:19:00.840 --> 00:19:01.890
attached to the post.

00:19:01.890 --> 00:19:03.690
And if this is the case,

00:19:03.690 --> 00:19:07.860
then this fold appears after
three lines of content.

00:19:07.860 --> 00:19:10.200
You see this year in the
left example, three lines,

00:19:10.200 --> 00:19:11.310
and then the fold appears.

00:19:11.310 --> 00:19:12.990
And if there's no attachment,

00:19:12.990 --> 00:19:15.600
this fold appears after five lines.

00:19:15.600 --> 00:19:17.010
So here the example to the right,

00:19:17.010 --> 00:19:18.660
you see four lines of text,

00:19:18.660 --> 00:19:20.670
but then there's also an empty line,

00:19:20.670 --> 00:19:22.290
an empty line, this counts as well.

00:19:22.290 --> 00:19:25.710
So after five lines, then
there will be the fold.

00:19:25.710 --> 00:19:26.970
So of course with your hook,

00:19:26.970 --> 00:19:29.370
you want to encourage people
to click on "see more."

00:19:29.370 --> 00:19:32.070
So maybe you are ending
with a question in the hook

00:19:32.070 --> 00:19:34.470
that then you are answering
in the remainder of the post,

00:19:34.470 --> 00:19:37.200
or maybe you make a rather
controversial statement

00:19:37.200 --> 00:19:40.170
that then you explain in
the remainder of the post.

00:19:40.170 --> 00:19:42.240
So encourage people to
click on "see more,"

00:19:42.240 --> 00:19:44.700
because of course, just the
fact alone that people click

00:19:44.700 --> 00:19:47.220
on "see more" is in itself already

00:19:47.220 --> 00:19:49.080
a positive sign to the algorithm

00:19:49.080 --> 00:19:51.330
that people find this post interesting,

00:19:51.330 --> 00:19:52.920
and they want to learn more about it.

00:19:52.920 --> 00:19:55.110
Let's now talk about another little hack

00:19:55.110 --> 00:19:57.180
that you can do in your content strategy

00:19:57.180 --> 00:19:58.950
to boost the reach of your post.

00:19:58.950 --> 00:20:01.200
And this is occasionally creating posts

00:20:01.200 --> 00:20:03.660
that really focus on boosting engagement,

00:20:03.660 --> 00:20:06.870
focus on getting as much
engagement as possible.

00:20:06.870 --> 00:20:09.960
And one type of post that
is very suited to do that

00:20:09.960 --> 00:20:11.040
are surveys.

00:20:11.040 --> 00:20:12.000
So you, in this example,

00:20:12.000 --> 00:20:13.740
you can see that I created a survey,

00:20:13.740 --> 00:20:16.470
it got about 40,000
impressions or 40,000 views.

00:20:16.470 --> 00:20:18.570
And there were about 2,000 people

00:20:18.570 --> 00:20:20.520
who participated in the survey

00:20:20.520 --> 00:20:23.010
who clicked on an option in the survey.

00:20:23.010 --> 00:20:26.130
So 2,000 people is quite
a lot for post of myself.

00:20:26.130 --> 00:20:27.600
So you can often see that surveys

00:20:27.600 --> 00:20:29.490
get quite a lot of engagement like this.

00:20:29.490 --> 00:20:32.070
And the good thing is
if a person interacted

00:20:32.070 --> 00:20:33.404
with your content in this way,

00:20:33.404 --> 00:20:37.080
even though this person did
not necessarily follow you,

00:20:37.080 --> 00:20:40.194
then this person is more
likely to, in the future,

00:20:40.194 --> 00:20:43.260
see posts that you
created, that you wrote,

00:20:43.260 --> 00:20:44.257
because LinkedIn now thinks that,

00:20:44.257 --> 00:20:46.920
"Hey, this person might be
interested in your content."

00:20:46.920 --> 00:20:48.210
So I would not encourage you

00:20:48.210 --> 00:20:50.387
to always only create posts like this.

00:20:50.387 --> 00:20:51.900
'Cause the truth is also

00:20:51.900 --> 00:20:54.510
only because someone
participated in a survey,

00:20:54.510 --> 00:20:56.130
doesn't necessarily mean that that person

00:20:56.130 --> 00:20:57.930
is really interested in your content.

00:20:57.930 --> 00:20:59.610
Doesn't necessarily
mean that another person

00:20:59.610 --> 00:21:01.830
will go to your profile and follow you.

00:21:01.830 --> 00:21:04.680
But occasional posts like this can help

00:21:04.680 --> 00:21:06.240
to increase your engagement,

00:21:06.240 --> 00:21:08.220
increase your views in the medium term.

00:21:08.220 --> 00:21:09.570
Just one word of caution.

00:21:09.570 --> 00:21:11.550
In the past, also earlier this year,

00:21:11.550 --> 00:21:13.950
LinkedIn was quite swamped with posts

00:21:13.950 --> 00:21:16.530
where people were doing surveys,
not with the survey tool,

00:21:16.530 --> 00:21:18.330
which I think is also
rather new in LinkedIn,

00:21:18.330 --> 00:21:22.020
but rather by abusing the
different types of like buttons,

00:21:22.020 --> 00:21:23.280
you could participate in the survey

00:21:23.280 --> 00:21:24.390
by clicking the like button

00:21:24.390 --> 00:21:26.280
or the insightful like button

00:21:26.280 --> 00:21:27.870
or the laugh like button and so on.

00:21:27.870 --> 00:21:28.947
And using that as a survey.

00:21:28.947 --> 00:21:31.290
And by that, of course
getting lots of engagement.

00:21:31.290 --> 00:21:34.320
So recently I've not really
seen any of these types of posts

00:21:34.320 --> 00:21:35.730
anymore on my timeline.

00:21:35.730 --> 00:21:36.960
So I think here, this is an example

00:21:36.960 --> 00:21:39.210
of how LinkedIn adjusted the algorithm

00:21:39.210 --> 00:21:41.100
to not publish these types of posts,

00:21:41.100 --> 00:21:41.933
which is why at the moment,

00:21:41.933 --> 00:21:44.370
I would not recommend you to
create this type of content.

00:21:44.370 --> 00:21:47.100
So let's now talk about another
strategy for your content.

00:21:47.100 --> 00:21:49.950
And this is the build in public strategy.

00:21:49.950 --> 00:21:51.330
Maybe you've already heard about it.

00:21:51.330 --> 00:21:53.070
There was quite a lot of buzz around it.

00:21:53.070 --> 00:21:54.510
And the main idea is this,

00:21:54.510 --> 00:21:56.580
especially suitable
for maybe entrepreneurs

00:21:56.580 --> 00:21:59.670
or anyone in leadership position
that you just talk about

00:21:59.670 --> 00:22:01.290
what you're building, about the company,

00:22:01.290 --> 00:22:03.030
the organization that you're building,

00:22:03.030 --> 00:22:05.130
and just regularly share
some insights on that.

00:22:05.130 --> 00:22:06.450
Maybe once per week,

00:22:06.450 --> 00:22:09.030
you share your biggest
learnings of the last week

00:22:09.030 --> 00:22:11.310
or the biggest achievements,
what you learn from them.

00:22:11.310 --> 00:22:13.740
Maybe also some failures,
what you learn from that.

00:22:13.740 --> 00:22:15.390
So this is just a strategy
where you can really

00:22:15.390 --> 00:22:17.550
lift the curtains, let people in,

00:22:17.550 --> 00:22:20.310
into your business and
provide value down the road.

00:22:20.310 --> 00:22:22.320
This can of course help to create trust

00:22:22.320 --> 00:22:25.170
with potential employees,
with potential customers.

00:22:25.170 --> 00:22:27.450
This is a great strategy
to create new leads.

00:22:27.450 --> 00:22:29.430
I'm just show you here an
example of a gentleman.

00:22:29.430 --> 00:22:31.920
So for full disclosure, I
don't know this gentleman.

00:22:31.920 --> 00:22:34.350
I also don't want to
endorse any of his content

00:22:34.350 --> 00:22:35.310
or his activities.

00:22:35.310 --> 00:22:37.710
I just thought this was a
nice example of where someone

00:22:37.710 --> 00:22:39.178
is doing exactly that.

00:22:39.178 --> 00:22:40.980
There are many other examples out there.

00:22:40.980 --> 00:22:43.320
So let's now talk about
some typical mistakes

00:22:43.320 --> 00:22:44.760
that many people are doing.

00:22:44.760 --> 00:22:47.430
And here I'm now referencing
this book from the great

00:22:47.430 --> 00:22:50.130
Gary Vaynerchuk, "Jab,
Jab, Jab, Right Hook."

00:22:50.130 --> 00:22:51.330
Maybe some of you have seen it.

00:22:51.330 --> 00:22:53.730
And the big notion of this book is that

00:22:53.730 --> 00:22:55.980
if you want to be
successful in social media,

00:22:55.980 --> 00:22:57.240
in the world out there,

00:22:57.240 --> 00:23:00.426
rather focus on the jabs
and be rather measured

00:23:00.426 --> 00:23:02.640
in your use of right hooks.

00:23:02.640 --> 00:23:06.480
And in this picture, the jab
is a piece of content posts

00:23:06.480 --> 00:23:09.690
that focuses on delivering
value for the audience.

00:23:09.690 --> 00:23:11.790
Whereas the right hook is the message,

00:23:11.790 --> 00:23:13.770
but you have some type
of commercial interest.

00:23:13.770 --> 00:23:17.095
Maybe you want someone to
become a customer of yourself.

00:23:17.095 --> 00:23:20.820
And as the title already says,
jab, jab, jab, right hook,

00:23:20.820 --> 00:23:24.120
right? So for every right hook
for every commercial message,

00:23:24.120 --> 00:23:25.950
make sure that there's a good number

00:23:25.950 --> 00:23:29.070
of really value creating
messages before that,

00:23:29.070 --> 00:23:30.090
or to say differently,

00:23:30.090 --> 00:23:33.240
your profile should not look
like a big advertisement.

00:23:33.240 --> 00:23:34.800
And this is frankly what I sometimes see.

00:23:34.800 --> 00:23:37.680
People also do wrong with
this built in public strategy

00:23:37.680 --> 00:23:40.290
where they just talk about
how great the organization is,

00:23:40.290 --> 00:23:41.550
how great their company is.

00:23:41.550 --> 00:23:44.130
This is not what people want
to read all of the time.

00:23:44.130 --> 00:23:47.220
In your content, focus on
delivering value for others.

00:23:47.220 --> 00:23:48.870
And if you do that consistently,

00:23:48.870 --> 00:23:50.700
then people will very much understand

00:23:50.700 --> 00:23:53.550
if you occasionally also
place this right hook

00:23:53.550 --> 00:23:54.900
with your own commercial interest.

00:23:54.900 --> 00:23:57.360
Let's now talk about sharing other posts,

00:23:57.360 --> 00:23:59.817
and in principle, there's
nothing wrong with that.

00:23:59.817 --> 00:24:02.310
You just need to be aware
that how the system,

00:24:02.310 --> 00:24:04.950
the algorithm works is that
if you share another post,

00:24:04.950 --> 00:24:07.950
that mainly helps the
reach of the other post.

00:24:07.950 --> 00:24:10.380
So the other post with an
often be shown to more people,

00:24:10.380 --> 00:24:12.960
potentially also to more
people in your audience.

00:24:12.960 --> 00:24:15.210
Build a post that you yourself create.

00:24:15.210 --> 00:24:16.590
By sharing another post,

00:24:16.590 --> 00:24:18.360
potentially also with some comments,

00:24:18.360 --> 00:24:21.240
this post in itself will often only get

00:24:21.240 --> 00:24:24.120
a fraction of the views than such a post.

00:24:24.120 --> 00:24:27.180
What usually get so sharing
other posts is great

00:24:27.180 --> 00:24:28.560
for the post that you're sharing,

00:24:28.560 --> 00:24:29.580
but often doesn't help you.

00:24:29.580 --> 00:24:31.620
If you want to create a post yourself,

00:24:31.620 --> 00:24:33.990
that gets lots of reach, lots of use.

00:24:33.990 --> 00:24:35.100
So depending on your goals,

00:24:35.100 --> 00:24:37.710
you might still want to share
the other post to support it,

00:24:37.710 --> 00:24:40.890
or you just decide to create
a new post by yourself

00:24:40.890 --> 00:24:42.780
that picks up some of the main messages

00:24:42.780 --> 00:24:44.970
and then has higher
chances to get the reach.

00:24:44.970 --> 00:24:47.610
Let's now also talk about
linking external resources,

00:24:47.610 --> 00:24:50.727
for instance, adding a link to
another website to your post.

00:24:50.727 --> 00:24:53.820
And here, the truth is
also that this is very bad

00:24:53.820 --> 00:24:55.470
for the reach of your post.

00:24:55.470 --> 00:24:57.660
I've recently seen an
analysis of another person

00:24:57.660 --> 00:24:58.493
with a conclusion,

00:24:58.493 --> 00:25:01.560
the post with external
links receive on average,

00:25:01.560 --> 00:25:05.490
only 1/6 of the reach of a
post without external links.

00:25:05.490 --> 00:25:07.500
And the reason for that I
think is also quite obvious.

00:25:07.500 --> 00:25:10.650
Of course, LinkedIn likes to
keep people on the platform.

00:25:10.650 --> 00:25:13.710
LinkedIn, doesn't like to
lead people from the platform,

00:25:13.710 --> 00:25:15.420
which is why they're punishing posts

00:25:15.420 --> 00:25:17.100
that have these external links.

00:25:17.100 --> 00:25:19.290
So my advice would be that
if you do want to link

00:25:19.290 --> 00:25:20.580
to an external page,

00:25:20.580 --> 00:25:22.800
don't put the link in the original post,

00:25:22.800 --> 00:25:25.110
but rather put the link in the comments

00:25:25.110 --> 00:25:26.887
and then you can write on
the post something like,

00:25:26.887 --> 00:25:28.920
"Oh, okay. Link to the
page and the comments."

00:25:28.920 --> 00:25:30.060
And this will then to some extent,

00:25:30.060 --> 00:25:31.860
bypass this reach penalty

00:25:31.860 --> 00:25:33.840
that LinkedIn otherwise
would put on your post.

00:25:33.840 --> 00:25:35.520
But now I would love to hear from you.

00:25:35.520 --> 00:25:39.390
Do you have any other LinkedIn
strategies and tips to share,

00:25:39.390 --> 00:25:41.370
leave a comment here in
the comments section.

00:25:41.370 --> 00:25:44.010
I'd love to get all your insights
or learn from you as well.

00:25:44.010 --> 00:25:46.380
Again, if you enjoyed it
or took any value from it,

00:25:46.380 --> 00:25:48.750
please hit the like
button for the algorithm,

00:25:48.750 --> 00:25:49.980
and also subscribe and follow

00:25:49.980 --> 00:25:51.540
to stay up to date on all the content.

